From b34bc1528d5ab7c32ae7fa468bfc265e552ba62b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huey <huey@carpetelam.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:03:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Support the NSO GameCube controller and add a raw packet
 capture

The GameCube controller advertises product ID 0x2073, which the scanner
didn't recognise, so it connected as an unknown side. A lone unknown
controller is treated as a sideways Joy-Con: its stick and D-pad were
rotated 90 degrees, its C-stick was never decoded, and L + R didn't
assign it. Handle it as a Pro Controller, which shares its report layout.

Parse the analog trigger bytes (0x3C/0x3D) into JoyconInput so they can
be verified on hardware before reaching the virtual gamepad.

Add an opt-in J2Raw log of packets whose input bytes changed, for
mapping controllers from a real capture.

